1
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:17,330
The wind favors us, Your Majesty.

2
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,919
If we continue to be blessed by the wind,

3
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,920
we should arrive at Ketil's farm
within two or three days.

4
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:33,220
I can't believe the king himself is
going to face a mere backcountry clan.

5
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:39,610
The Jomsvikings could've handled this.

6
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:45,620
His Majesty has
a well thought-out plan, Floki.

7
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:50,360
A good liegeman doesn't question
his king's decisions.

8
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:56,630
Jomsborg is an ally.
I am not quite his liegeman.

9
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:59,770
Don't forget that, Ulf.

10
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:07,260
Do you suppose Ketil and his family
will oppose the king?

11
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:10,120
I'm not sure.

12
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,820
I've heard Ketil is a mighty warrior who used
to be known as the Iron Fist on the battlefield.

13
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:16,680
We mustn't underestimate him.

14
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:21,080
He didn't seem that way to me.

15
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:26,730
People are assets. I'd hate to waste them.

16
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:33,160
It would be best if Ketil's family
submitted to the king's authority.

17
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:37,350
Is that why you're going there in person?

18
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:42,479
But they've committed
an outrage against you.

19
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:46,870
Shouldn't we make an example
out of them by punishing them harshly?

20
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:51,720
I intend to show no mercy if they defy me.

21
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:07,090
A tailwind...

22
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:13,760
But the waves are tall,
and the land we seek is far ahead.

23
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,790
The First Method.

24
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:06,480
The First Method.

25
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:12,860
Oh, my. I thought Master Ketil
had returned, but it's Mister Thorgil.

26
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:19,610
Welcome back, Mister Thorgil.

27
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:23,290
Thanks. I brought you a gift. Take this.

28
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,450
Yah!

29
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,260
Master!

30
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:41,259
Get him a stiff drink and let him sleep.

31
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:44,469
What a hopeless old man.

32
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:47,319
Come on, retainers.

33
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,869
This is no time to be hanging fish to dry.

34
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,480
We're preparing for battle.

35
00:04:51,950 --> 00:04:57,789
Enemy forces will be arriving soon
to take this entire farm.

36
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:00,740
Gather all the men and
weapons you can find.

37
00:05:04,230 --> 00:05:07,079
Wh-What? Enemy? Who?

38
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,999
How soon is soon?

39
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,229
What's wrong with the master?

40
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,265
What happened to him?

41
00:05:11,266 --> 00:05:13,040
Hey, wait. Mister Thorgil...

42
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:17,069
Let us conclude our deal before the battle.

43
00:05:17,070 --> 00:05:19,110
We don't want to get
caught up in the fighting.

44
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:25,060
Talk to my dad about that. I'm busy.

45
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:29,060
Olmar, hurry up.

46
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:33,189
This is your first battle.

47
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:36,090
Stick by me and learn to fight.

48
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:42,490
Though considering who we're up against,
this might be our last battle.

49
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:47,149
Aren't you pleased, Olmar?

50
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:49,800
You're finally getting to fight,
just like you wanted.

51
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:58,330
Mister Ketil, pull yourself together.

52
00:05:59,050 --> 00:06:03,760
Didn't you say you'd buy our cargo
at triple market price?

53
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:08,370
That's why we transported
your family all the way here.

54
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:14,230
Arnheid...

55
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:16,040
What?

56
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:30,700
H-Hey, wait. Ketil.

57
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:33,690
Wait a minute, Ketil.

58
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:36,970
Please, Ketil!

59
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,570
I'm sure it'll be fine.

60
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,920
You've got a good
feeling about this, right?

61
00:06:49,850 --> 00:06:53,140
This time, it'll be the real Thorfinn.

62
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:59,560
You're right.

63
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:03,530
I'll choose to believe that's true.

64
00:07:08,910 --> 00:07:11,870
A battle? Here?

65
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,489
In a few days, apparently.

66
00:07:14,490 --> 00:07:18,189
Mister Thorgil said to repair
the fortress walls.

67
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:21,209
Repair the walls? But...

68
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:24,569
This can't be fixed in just a few days.

69
00:07:24,570 --> 00:07:26,550
Who are we fighting, anyway?

70
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,429
He wouldn't say.

71
00:07:29,430 --> 00:07:32,199
He said he'd tell us
once the soldiers were gathered.

72
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,680
Doesn't matter who we're fighting.
We can't win.

73
00:07:35,070 --> 00:07:39,890
There aren't enough
experienced soldiers on this farm.

74
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:45,280
Just the other day,
we lost five valuable fighters.

75
00:07:47,590 --> 00:07:51,300
The guests look unsettled about something.

76
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:54,570
Has the master returned?

77
00:07:57,070 --> 00:08:03,870
I wonder what he's going to do
when he learns Arnheid tried to escape.

78
00:08:09,750 --> 00:08:13,030
You think he'll punish her?

79
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:18,820
A lot of people died.

80
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:25,810
But the master adores Arnheid.

81
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:30,420
He won't go too hard on her, will he?

82
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:37,990
Maybe. She's pregnant with his child, too.

83
00:08:42,450 --> 00:08:47,370
I'm worried. I hope she's all right.

84
00:08:49,510 --> 00:08:50,550
I'm sorry.

85
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:59,970
You fought Snake and his men
for Arnheid and Gardar, right?

86
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:05,510
You even broke your oath.

87
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:14,330
Sometimes you have to fight.

88
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:18,330
Thank you, Thorfinn.

89
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,940
I like Snake.

90
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:30,710
He's a kind and principled man.

91
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:36,290
I didn't want to fight him.

92
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:41,670
And in the end, I let Gardar die.

93
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:53,210
I'm stupid, so I'm not sure how to say it.

94
00:09:55,040 --> 00:10:00,120
But I wonder if there wasn't a better way.

95
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,779
Did so many people have to get hurt?

96
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:07,540
Did people have to lose their lives?

97
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:12,710
Did I try to find a way to avoid that?

98
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,730
There wasn't one.

99
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:22,360
After all the guests that died,
Snake couldn't back down, either.

100
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:30,820
But violence should be a last resort.

101
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:40,500
I wonder what the best option was, though.

102
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:45,700
What should've been tried first?

103
00:10:48,530 --> 00:10:55,570
I want to learn to find that first method.

104
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:03,670
There is no person who deserves to be hurt.

105
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,070
You're right.

106
00:11:12,830 --> 00:11:14,310
That's exactly right.

107
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:35,550
Arnheid, where are you? Arnheid...

108
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,660
Where are you?

109
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,539
My, what a surprise.

110
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:53,510
You're back early, dear husband.

111
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:59,830
I heard King Harald passed away.

112
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,580
Dear?

113
00:12:07,310 --> 00:12:09,580
A-Arnheid...

114
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:19,669
That shameless slave has been
tied up and thrown in the stable.

115
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:24,220
She caused quite a lot of
trouble while you were gone.

116
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:33,700
She was plotting to escape.
What a truly ungrateful slave.

117
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:38,450
Escape?

118
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,770
Arnheid tried to...

119
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:49,049
Her old flame came to the farm
and led her away.

120
00:12:49,050 --> 00:12:51,750
Many of the guests died.

121
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:58,010
Two of our male slaves even helped them.

122
00:12:58,430 --> 00:13:00,570
What an unbelievable woman.

123
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:07,530
You'll have to address
this matter properly, dear.

124
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:11,190
Escape...

125
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:18,870
Why?

126
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:25,380
Why does everything
keep slipping from my grasp?

127
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:29,990
Escape?

128
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,630
Why?

129
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:50,630
Nobody told me anything about that.

130
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,560
I can't let you see him.

131
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:56,329
But it's true.

132
00:13:56,330 --> 00:14:00,190
Ketil promised to free Thorfinn.

133
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,509
In any case,
I'd like to at least see his face.

134
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:08,330
I want to know if the man you've
got here is the Thorfinn I'm looking for.

135
00:14:08,870 --> 00:14:11,350
Not until I've gotten confirmation
from the master.

136
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:17,960
Otherwise I can't allow anyone
to meet with someone who's locked up.

137
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:22,130
Fine. I understand.

138
00:14:24,950 --> 00:14:30,220
Come with me. Let's go talk to Ketil.

139
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:35,639
I'm sorry to bother you
when you're so busy, Pater.

140
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:39,610
I don't mind showing you around, but...

141
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:46,740
Is there a problem?

142
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:54,750
As an outsider, you're the only one
I can turn to for help with this matter.

143
00:14:56,850 --> 00:15:03,000
Forgive me, Mister Leif, but can you
spare the funds to purchase a slave?

144
00:15:04,230 --> 00:15:10,570
Some, I suppose. I was promised
I could have Thorfinn for free.

145
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:14,640
The master keeps his promises.

146
00:15:15,490 --> 00:15:19,650
Thorfinn and Einar will be fine.

147
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:23,770
But Arnheid is a more challenging matter.

148
00:15:27,490 --> 00:15:32,230
I know I'm asking for a lot, Mister Leif,

149
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:38,820
but would you be willing to
purchase two slaves besides Thorfinn?

150
00:15:54,110 --> 00:15:55,670
Arnheid...

151
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,589
Man, I'm bored.

152
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:11,830
I've got a woman right in front of me,
and I can't even do anything with her.

153
00:16:16,950 --> 00:16:22,469
You act all meek, but you actually
know what you're doing, don't you?

154
00:16:22,470 --> 00:16:28,300
The master will spank you a few times
and forgive you for everything.

155
00:16:29,010 --> 00:16:32,800
He's too easy on you.

156
00:16:36,260 --> 00:16:41,310
You're lucky your punishment
wasn't up to us guests.

157
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:52,320
By now you'd have been
stripped naked and raped by all of us

158
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:56,950
for our brothers who were killed.

159
00:16:58,430 --> 00:17:03,010
Our dead brothers wouldn't be
able to rest in peace otherwise.

160
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,360
Don't you agree?

161
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:10,550
What are you doing?

162
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:15,130
S-Sir, you're back.

163
00:17:21,610 --> 00:17:27,189
Leave. I have business with Arnheid.

164
00:17:27,190 --> 00:17:30,379
But sir, I, uh...

165
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,699
Leave.

166
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:33,590
Y-Yes, sir.

167
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:46,210
You tried to escape from me?

168
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:51,490
Why, Arnheid?

169
00:17:52,090 --> 00:17:53,330
Why?

170
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:10,330
Why?

171
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:14,470
Why don't you understand?

172
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:18,250
Why would you do that?

173
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:25,170
Do you despise me?

174
00:18:28,750 --> 00:18:32,200
I won't allow anyone to
take my pride from me.

175
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:39,620
Not even you, Arnheid.

176
00:18:45,570 --> 00:18:49,270
Stop... N-Not my stomach...

177
00:18:50,550 --> 00:18:53,280
I have a child inside me...

178
00:18:56,350 --> 00:19:00,129
I have a child inside me.

179
00:19:00,130 --> 00:19:03,080
Please, no more.

180
00:19:07,110 --> 00:19:08,810
Whose child is it?

181
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:15,449
I s-s-swear it's yours, Master.

182
00:19:15,450 --> 00:19:18,050
It's true. Please believe me.

183
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:22,010
Believe you?

184
00:19:25,490 --> 00:19:31,370
You... You were the only one I trusted.

185
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:39,820
What am I supposed to believe, huh?

186
00:19:40,190 --> 00:19:42,580
What does it mean to trust someone?

187
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:46,080
It's true? It's real?

188
00:19:46,630 --> 00:19:54,630
I won't suffer losing something
I never doubted!

189
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,590
You'll pay for this, you thieves!

190
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:03,220
With this hand, I will punish you!

191
00:20:10,590 --> 00:20:11,850
Arnheid!

192
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:22,770
Given the weight of Arnheid's crimes,
it makes sense to flog her.

193
00:20:23,830 --> 00:20:27,140
But if you keep hitting her,
you'll be executing her.

194
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:31,410
Arnheid is your slave, sir.

195
00:20:31,870 --> 00:20:35,130
You have the right to kill her.

196
00:20:36,190 --> 00:20:38,120
You want to execute her, right?

197
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:42,250
Then I'll let go of the rod.

198
00:21:05,110 --> 00:21:07,810
Tend her wounds, Pater.

199
00:21:13,620 --> 00:21:14,600
Scary...

200
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:23,730
K-Ketil, if you don't want that slave girl,
would you sell her to me?

201
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:30,909
I heard you have
two other slaves besides Thorfinn.

202
00:21:30,910 --> 00:21:33,450
That they're Thorfinn's friends.

203
00:21:33,890 --> 00:21:35,540
I'll pay.

204
00:21:36,610 --> 00:21:38,600
I'd like to buy them from you.

205
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,160
Who said I don't want her?

206
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:53,880
Take Thorfinn and Einar wherever you want.

207
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,750
But I'm not selling Arnheid.

208
00:21:59,470 --> 00:22:04,330
That woman belongs to me.

209
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:36,770
She's alive, but she's still unconscious.

210
00:22:38,090 --> 00:22:40,790
I don't know if she'll make it.

211
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:50,289
Don't touch her, Einar.

212
00:22:50,290 --> 00:22:52,060
You mustn't move her.

213
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:05,930
They won't get away with this.

214
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:09,570
They're all thieves.

215
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:12,599
I raised it up with such care.

216
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:15,159
I take such good care of it.

217
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,210
And they're trying to take it all from me.

218
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:20,929
Dad, where have you been?

219
00:23:20,930 --> 00:23:23,430
We've got a mountain of things to do.

220
00:23:24,710 --> 00:23:26,950
Also, a suit of armor would be...

221
00:23:27,430 --> 00:23:29,220
Hey, Dad.

222
00:23:35,650 --> 00:23:38,840
Those thieves won't get away with this.

223
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:41,050
I'll punish them.

224
00:23:46,770 --> 00:23:51,570
Even if it's the king.

225
00:25:36,180 --> 00:25:38,055
The Battle of Ketil's Farm.

226
00:25:37,220 --> 00:25:39,480
"The Battle of Ketil's Farm."

227
00:25:38,056 --> 00:25:39,930
The Battle of Ketil's Farm.
